  "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\u27e84{t}^{2}-3t,\\,5{e}^{2t}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4{t}^{2}-3t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}5{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int (4{t}^{2}-3t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int 5{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t=5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}=\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\u27e84{t}^{2}-3t,\\,5{e}^{2t}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8(\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2},\\,(\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{2t}){|}_{0}^{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(\\frac{4}{3}(8)-\\frac{3}{2}(4))-0,\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(\\frac{32}{3}-6),\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{14}{3},\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{14}{3},\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
